## Frozen correction re-review — S02 addressed; S01 remains narrowly blocked

Reviewed frozen tool `3619ab8dfe977c4f1ea7b8dc016f17353fd7f09a2c11b4c35a7077af8e1c54f0`, tests `487e3d8531c8f2d5a98b3f785bb570b2599e8f476d87644f62d170517194b95c` and operations `d9dfc0f2b0662c0de5e36a0b9de2ca3dea35923b18e30063e19bf4cccddd3f19`. Root application/tool/fixture remains unchanged; correction is still unintegrated. The original rejection and probes above remain historical evidence.

The original S01 unit proofImage route now refuses before custody publication. The revision closes manifest and distinct beforeRoot/originalBaseline wrappers, canonical encoded count nodes, discriminated proof images, raw heads, receipt/target fields and bounded scratch maps. Exact known fields and nullable branches preserve genuine generated proofs; no generic codec or public data schema was introduced. Original independent malformed-proof probe now returns failed-precondition/count-encoded-purpose with zero DB IO.

S02 is addressed on this frozen source: both actual full exports reject own public now options before any mutation; fullContext uses runtime Date.now. The original independent owner takeover probe now refuses both apply and restore with count-public-clock-unavailable and zero new writes. A different owner without a supplied clock receives count-lease-busy while the actual runtime lease is live. Existing early bootstrap/store interfaces remain; private IPC actors scope only their validated finite nowMs through Date.now inside the child and restore it in finally. This is source/model control evidence, not native SDK lease acceptance.

**Remaining S01 defect: authenticated local replay cursor types.** validateReplayState at 445-465 whitelists lastEpisode/lastHead but does not validate their values as existing opaque-ID-or-null and hash-or-null types. An independent probe used the genuine current private AEAD head after actual exported apply over existing isolated MemoryFirestore. Using the synthetic fixture's actual key/custody, it changed lastEpisode to a synthetic object containing content/authorId and lastHead to an array, retained every other field and exact release binding, then authenticated the ciphertext normally. Actual apply with maxItems 1 returned in-progress and republished both invalid fields in a new encrypted revision. Firestore writes added: 0. This is malformed authenticated-state/privacy acceptance, not no-key access, forged active proof or a claim that final proof digests can be bypassed.

Permanent tests-only patch `/tmp/hudhud-b15-replay-cursor-tests.patch` (`209fee8bfddb7fee9760655f4823ac6a3028f5bc515dee7389b8667a9038a1a5`) adds two actual custody rejection cases and a genuine null/string progress control without modifying source. Correct isolated baseline: 3 tests, 1 control PASS, 2 intended Missing expected rejection FAIL, 0 skips, 11989.21246 ms. Test candidate `6e2981b27228c1636b57673dbcad1ea076dc642e9a223980995d6353ef57f985` is isolated at `/tmp/hudhud-b15-cursor-regression`; source remains 3619. An earlier mistaken path ran zero selected cases and is retained explicitly INVALID, earning no RED credit. Parent independently reruns the correct baseline before authorizing a fix.

The consolidated accepted-wire field/type/null/phase matrix is `/tmp/hudhud-b15-final-schema-matrix.md` (`7560990c0469993978c836511cdd1609b638617992bbc107861567a8fc2528c5`). It also lists static early-type omissions in plan, completion and receipt fields, including nullable progress/controller hashes and restore predecessor pairs. Those are NOT independently demonstrated bypasses: downstream native/controller/backup/final digest checks may already reject them. Preserve every downstream check. Any new validation must have pre-fix permanent typed/null/phase guard tests and genuine controls; already-rejected mutations are guard coverage, never invented RED. No field/wire expansion is needed.

Independent focused correction/security/protocol checks: 25/25 PASS, 0 fail/skip, 145977.955844 ms. This includes the revised permanent review regressions and valid controls plus custody/IPC/publication guards. Original independent probes now verify refusal and runtime lease preservation. Full 81 author gate is still a separate running obligation at this review cutpoint; no full result or native SDK acceptance is inferred. Source/schema review remains CHANGES REQUIRED until the remaining cursor pair and consolidated guard coverage are corrected, frozen and independently re-reviewed. SDK patches remain prepared/unintegrated, production remains refused, and no task/finding is CLOSED.


